v0.1.8 — Secondary LLM Provider + Memories Tab

Features:
- Secondary LLM provider per provider: after tool calls (HA commands,
  web search, skills), the secondary provider generates the final
  response — useful for cost reduction or faster processing with
  large local models
- Provider modal: new "Secondary Provider" dropdown to select a
  secondary provider for each configured provider
- Provider cards show secondary provider badge when configured
- New top-level "Memories" tab: view, add, filter, bulk-delete and
  manage memories grouped by user — no longer inside the user modal
- User modal simplified: shows stats and API key only

Changes:
- services/providers.py: added get_secondary_provider() function
- routers/chat.py: tool re-call uses secondary provider (both
  streaming and non-streaming paths)
- static/index.html: new Memories panel, secondary provider dropdown
  in provider modal, removed memory sections from user modal
- static/js/app.js: memories tab functions, secondary provider
  populate/save/edit/render, switchToTab updated
- static/js/i18n.js: EN/RO translations for all new elements
- static/css/style.css: secondary provider badge styling
- core/config.py: version bump to v0.1.8
